2. THE MODEL WEIGHTS  —  Qwen RESEARCH LICENCE (NON-COMMERCIAL)
===============================================================================

The submitted model (`alamz-tech-sme-copilot-Q4_K_M.gguf`, distributed via
Hugging Face) is a QLoRA fine-tune of **Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct** and is therefore
a derivative work governed by the Qwen RESEARCH LICENSE AGREEMENT, NOT by the
MIT licence above.

  Qwen is licensed under the Qwen RESEARCH LICENSE AGREEMENT,
  Copyright (c) Alibaba Cloud. All Rights Reserved.
  https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct/blob/main/LICENSE

  Built with Qwen.

Key term: the Qwen Research Licence permits use, reproduction, distribution and
derivative works **FOR NON-COMMERCIAL PURPOSES ONLY**. Commercial use requires a
separate licence request to Alibaba Cloud.

Modifications made to the base model:
  - QLoRA fine-tune (rank 32, all layers) on an SME back-office corpus and a
    Nigeria-2025 tax fact base
  - Fusion of the adapter and quantization to GGUF Q4_K_M with a
    domain-calibrated importance matrix

WHY THIS MATTERS AND WHAT IS PLANNED
The base model was selected on measured accuracy before its licence terms were
fully examined; the restriction was identified on 2026-08-11 and is disclosed
here rather than left implicit. Because the deterministic engine, the data
pipeline and the evaluation harnesses are all base-model-agnostic (MIT above),
migrating to a permissively licensed base is a contained change: retrain,
re-run the three gates, rebuild. `build/mlx_lora_config.phi.yaml` holds a
prepared configuration for Phi-3.5-mini-instruct (MIT) for exactly that purpose.
Any commercial deployment will either follow that migration or obtain a
commercial licence from Alibaba Cloud first.
